      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Pseudoaneurysm is an unusual complication of myocardial infarction. Although its pathogenesis is known, the course of the condition is obscure. The diagnosis is usually made post-mortally. We present a case of a pseudoaneurysm following a myocardial infarction, diagnosed at a routine polyclinical echocardiographic examination in a patient who at the time of diagnosis was free of symptoms. The patient was successfully operated upon."},
